Subject: Cantor B1 A8 Production Broker Projection Correspondence Threat Review

@ [threat_review_uuid] e611462d-b11d-490b-b5dc-ab1f0374b5f0

& [Threats]
  + confused deputy turns correspondence into activation; endpoint or module smuggling turns inert identifiers into capability; digest laundering claims broker existence
  + nested A7 truncation hides missing permit; forged comparison or false authority promotes broker presence; echo leaks hostile or secret text
  + path link junction reparse traversal and resource abuse escape evidence boundary; concurrent replacement undermines atomicity claims

& [Controls]
  + no dynamic consumer, resolver, client, callback, network, subprocess, environment, path or writer in production; conservative identifier grammar and non-echo errors
  + full predecessor reconstruction every-field receipt validation manifest-first hashes stable direct files strict bounds and explicit zero-effect/false-authority assertions

& [Residual]
  + supplied metadata may be false and stable-file reads are not universally atomic; receipts name both limits and never claim live broker state
